meta {
  name: 9c. Verify Gateway Auth (unauthenticated)
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

get {
  url: {{apisixApiUrl}}/v1/datasets/{{sagaDataSetId}}/{{sagaSlug}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

tests {
  test("Unauthenticated request to a protected dataset is denied (401)", function() {
    // openid-connect passes the anonymous request through (unauth_action: pass); OPA denies it
    // because the dataset is not open-data (missing_user_context → 401 via deny_status).
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(401);
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 9c of 18** — Verify APISIX gateway enforces authentication on the published-API host.

  Sends an unauthenticated GET request to the per-named-API data route `api.<host>/v1/datasets/{id}/{slug}` through the APISIX gateway. The OpenID-Connect plugin applied by the saga must reject the request with 401.

  **Precondition:** `sagaDataSetId` is set; APISIX reachable at `apisixApiUrl` (whose hostname matches the `hosts` filter on the saga-provisioned route); saga has completed and the route exists.

  **Expected Response:** 401 Unauthorized (no bearer token provided).

  **Issue #1368:** Published data API is isolated from the management API via a configured API virtual host — the request must hit the FROST route on `api.<host>` and be rejected by auth, not by path mismatch.
}
